# What the dev watcher must not restart the app over.
#
# `beforeDevCommand` is `npm run bundle:runtime`, and that script writes into
# two directories inside this one: `resources/`, where the bootstrap scripts and
# the client plugin are staged, and `installer/`, where the NSIS bitmaps are
# drawn. Both are rewritten unconditionally on every run — a copy rather than a
# comparison, deliberately, so that a stale copy of the thing that installs
# everything else cannot happen.
#
# The watcher sees those writes as source changes and rebuilds. So `npm run dev`
# opened the app, then closed it and opened it again, once per staged directory,
# every single time. `tauri build` never did, because nothing is watching there
# — which is what made this look like an app bug rather than a watcher one.
#
# The rule these two share is the one to apply to anything added later: they are
# build output that happens to live under `src-tauri/`, and both are in
# `.gitignore` for exactly that reason. Generated output does not belong to the
# watcher. Source that is staged *into* these directories — `scripts/` and
# `plugin/` at the repository root — is outside `src-tauri/` and was never
# watched to begin with, so nothing is lost here: editing either one still means
# re-running `npm run dev`, as it always did.
#
# `target/` and `gen/` are not listed. The CLI ignores those on its own.

resources/
installer/
